.TH NETPULSE 1 "November 2026" "netpulse 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netpulse \- network diagnostics in a desktop window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netpulse
[\fB\-\-browser\fR | \fB\-\-no\-open\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.br
.B netpulse
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netpulse
is a local, single-user network diagnostics tool. It runs the real system tools
(ping, traceroute, mtr, dig, nslookup, host, whois, curl, openssl, ip, ss, resolvectl)
and shows their output live in a graphical interface, together with a parsed summary.
.PP
The interface is served by a small web server that listens on the loopback interface
only. It opens in a native GTK window when GTK 4, WebKitGTK 6.0 and PyGObject are
installed, and in the default web browser otherwise.
.PP
Starting
.B netpulse
again while it is running raises the existing window (or opens the existing session in
the browser) instead of starting a second copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-browser
Open the interface in the default web browser instead of a native window. In this mode
NetPulse stops by itself about two minutes after the browser page is closed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open anything; print the address (including the access token) and keep running
until interrupted.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Listen on \fIPORT\fR instead of a random free port.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDRESS"
Listen on another loopback address (default 127.0.0.1). Non-loopback addresses are refused.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log HTTP requests to standard error (the access token is redacted).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH SECURITY
A random access token is created at every start and required for every API request.
Requests with an unexpected Host or Origin header are refused, which blocks DNS
rebinding and requests from other web pages. Tools are always started without a shell,
with validated arguments. NetPulse never asks for root privileges.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/netpulse/settings.json
Settings (theme, history size). Default: \fI~/.config/netpulse/\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/netpulse/history.jsonl
Run history. Default: \fI~/.local/share/netpulse/\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/netpulse/
Lock file and address of the running instance.
.SH PRIVACY
NetPulse has no telemetry and no update checks. It only contacts the hosts you test.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the server could not start or a running instance does not answer,
2 for invalid command-line options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR traceroute (8),
.BR tracepath (8),
.BR mtr (8),
.BR dig (1),
.BR nslookup (1),
.BR host (1),
.BR whois (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR openssl-s_client (1ssl),
.BR ip (8),
.BR ss (8),
.BR resolvectl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/agent-denis/netpulse/issues
